{
  "title": "Add raw scalar output support to the glom CLI",
  "instruction": "Support scalar / raw output in the glom command-line interface. When executing glom queries and transformations from the CLI, users should be able to specify a raw/scalar output option (e.g. `--raw` / `-r`) so that scalar results (such as strings, numbers, booleans, or null/None) are printed directly as raw unquoted text rather than JSON-encoded strings with surrounding quotes. If the transformation result is a container or collection (such as a dictionary, list, or other non-scalar mapping/sequence), the output should fall back to standard JSON output formatting."
}
